# Firebase. The service account key is a private key with admin rights on the project and
# must never be committed — it belongs in EAS credentials, not in the repo.
#
# google-services.json IS tracked, deliberately. It holds no private key: the api_key in it is
# a client key scoped to the package name and signing certificate, and the whole file ships
# inside every APK, so it is readable by anyone holding the build. It has to be tracked because
# EAS Build uploads only the files git knows about — ignoring it fails the build with
# "google-services.json is missing" at the Google Services gradle step.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
